{
  "analysis": "Doom boots and loads the WAD but fails at R_Init with Z_Malloc trying to allocate 25,145,144 bytes, exceeding the 6MB zone. The zone size 0x600000 (6MB) is correct per DEFAULT_RAM=6. I need to see the full R_InitTextures function to find the failing allocation and determine if there is an interpreter bug causing incorrect numtextures or size computation.",
  "plan": "Inspect the full R_InitTextures function, especially Z_Malloc calls, and check numtextures computation. Then add VM tracing to log Z_Malloc sizes and callers to identify the source of the 25MB allocation.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '350,520p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_data.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -s /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -E \"Z_Malloc|R_InitTextures|numtextures\" | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"numtextures\\|texturecolumnlump\\|texturecolumnofs\\|texturecomposite\\|Z_Malloc.*sizeof\\|malloc\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_data.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
